commit 56cd8016ae9f6b36ec565bf3e70fc6537008761e

C03: a trailing means directive («Usa Python.») is declined as envelope and the system reading is reported without claiming it (SYSTEM1545)

H0076 «Dime que version de Windows tengo y cuanta RAM tiene este PC. Usa Python.» reached no reader: the second sentence is not a request and broke the resolution, and SYSTEM1028 measured the candidate of the time asking for a terminal to run a script. The owner does not want the assistant to program as a capability; the reading comes from its own observation. effect_intent.py strips a trailing means directive (usa/usá/con/mediante + Python, PowerShell, a script, code, the terminal) only behind a request and exposes it as declined_means; llm.py instructs that the values were read directly and vetoes a final that says it used or ran that means, a script or code, or asks for a terminal (claimed_means); a negated mention («sin Python») is the honest disclaimer, not a claim. Registry-wide recogniser diff: only H0076 changes (None → system.status).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>


